BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//WebMS Intra//Test fixture//EN
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: INTERVAL is honoured. The first event is every SECOND Thursday, the
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:second every THIRD month. If INTERVAL were ignored both would repeat far too often - a
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:fortnightly rota would appear every week, which is the sort of mistake nobody reports
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:because the extra dates look perfectly ordinary.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:interval-weekly-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260903T180000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260903T190000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;INTERVAL=2;BYDAY=TH;COUNT=5
SUMMARY:Fortnightly rota
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:interval-monthly-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260910T120000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260910T130000
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;INTERVAL=3;COUNT=4
SUMMARY:Quarterly review
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
